$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=ang180pos  LOC_AFTER=?
$( If the angle at ` A ` of the triangle with vertices ` A ` , ` B ` , ` C ` ,
   measured from ` ( B - A ) ` to ` ( C - A ) ` , lies in ` ( 0 (,) _pi ) ` ,
   so that the triangle is positively oriented, then so do its angles at ` B `
   and at ` C ` taken in the same cyclic order, and the three angles sum to `
   _pi ` . ` F ` is the signed angle function, as in ~ ang2exp . $)

$d A x
$d A y
$d B x
$d B y
$d C x
$d C y
$d x y

h1::ang180pos.1  |- F = ( x e. ( CC \ { 0 } ) , y e. ( CC \ { 0 } ) |-> ( Im ` ( log ` ( y / x ) ) ) )
